{"title":"2009 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Emily sets up a lemonade stand. She has set-up costs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/59309bdf3e8c0ecbdbe60888412cbbf38bd3e6b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$12.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> and each cup of lemonade costs her <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90dfbdbe7579b90dd9628d52d693f145426a423e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> to make. She sells each cup of lemonade for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a52990ff1664f1102b7b1fac4e7b2106f5e0728.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the number of cups that she must sell to break even (that is, to have a profit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de5552aa8609c6804707c747d7b7aba076e1f740.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />)?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of cups she needs to sell to get a profit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/6/2e613b3373afb0ef69270ae63f1252a2d309aa26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. Since each cup of lemonade costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90dfbdbe7579b90dd9628d52d693f145426a423e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> to make and Emily sells each cup for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a52990ff1664f1102b7b1fac4e7b2106f5e0728.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, Emily earns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/5124eb1e5bb43ebdd3efd2e68163bc9bae35f5de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.75 - \\$0.15 = \\$0.60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"173\" height=\"17\" /> net per cup of lemonade. \n</p><p>However, her set-up costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/59309bdf3e8c0ecbdbe60888412cbbf38bd3e6b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$12.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />, meaning that the money that she earned net outside of the set-up cost must be the same as the set-up cost, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/c/09cb4630dd7ba2998732010ac98ddc47c96f41d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.60c = 12.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a92cbf386563c90ce25be9a7281bfaad06a8f69f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\frac{12.00}{0.60} = \\boxed{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017221553\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.017 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 48/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 315/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2164/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.573      1 2009_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    8.573      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36999:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017221553 and revision id 285933. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}